'''Battle''': Immediately spawn Cleanerbot, then spawn Manic Lion when you can afford him so that you can stall the Elder Sloth. You may upgrade your Worker Cat while stalling, and spawn a Fishman, but try to make sure it doesn't instantly die to Elder Sloth or Mina.

After the boss wave hits, you can start spawning the non combo units. Try to time them all so that Mina doesn't hit them, although this may be difficult in Cleanerbot's case. Manic Lion should be spawned such that it can act as a frontline when there is no Cleanerbot. Maglev should be spawned either after or slightly before Elder Sloth attacks, as this will maximise the amount of times it is hit by Mr. Mole. Timing Maglev is important, as Mr. Mole's knockback can help every one to chain a lot of its extremely powerful attacks and take off a significant portion of Elder Sloth's HP. Minimise use of the [[Cat Cannon]] while Elder Sloth is alive, so that you don't sync the Mr. Moles.

Hopefully, Elder Sloth should fall before Mina is in range of the base. Spawn Bahamut to speed up the process of Tackey removal, then you should just be left with Mina and the Moles. If you have any cats in the blindspot of the Moles and are attacking Mina, do '''not''' use the Cat Cannon. Otherwise, try and use it to get at least a single Manic Lion in the blindspot. Doing so essentially wins the stage, as the only other enemy that can spawn is a single [[Ms. Sign]]. Once Mina is dead, the rest of the stage is completely trivial.

